#### keeps cold orchestration stdout out of the strict release transcript

- Verify: keeps cold orchestration stdout out of the strict release transcript
   - Expected: code equals `0)  # oracle: the runner exits cleanly`
   - Expected: stdout does not contain `Compiled `
   - Expected: stdout does not contain `GUI_SMF_WRAP `


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 14 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-APP-GUIPERF-001
step("Verify: keeps cold orchestration stdout out of the strict release transcript")
# Runtime oracle: executing the real evidence runner emits exactly one
# strict evidence row on stdout (a skip row on non-mac hosts) — no cold
# orchestration chatter ("Compiled ...", shell noise) leaks into the
# transcript stream the release gate consumes.
val bin = "/mnt/data/worktrees/simple-main/bin/simple"
val (stdout, _stderr, code) = process_run(bin, ["run", "/tmp/land11/src/app/gui_perf/macos_smf_dynlib_evidence.spl"])
expect(code).to_equal(0)  # oracle: the runner exits cleanly
val selected = gui_mac_smf_dynlib_select_stdout_row(stdout, "GUI_MAC_SMF_DYNLIB_EVIDENCE")
expect(selected).to_contain("status=skip")  # oracle: non-mac host reports an explicit skip
expect(selected).to_contain("requires-macos-arm64")
expect(stdout.contains("Compiled ")).to_equal(false)  # oracle: compile chatter stays off stdout
expect(stdout.contains("GUI_SMF_WRAP ")).to_equal(false)  # oracle: wrapper chatter stays off stdout
```

</details>

